==English==

===Etymology===
From Hindi ''cāṭ'' चाट (tasting, a delicacy), from ''cāṭnā'' चाटना (to lick), from [[Prakrit]] ''caṭṭei'' चट्टेइ (to devour with relish, eat noisily).

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɑːt|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# any [[savory]] [[snack]], sold from a [[roadside]] [[stall]] in [[India]], or served as a [[starter]] in an Indian restaurant

